Sure!  Loops are used to execute a sequence of instructions multiple times.  They can be used with if/then statements to repeatedly do something, or with loops to execute code structures over and over.  They can also be used with conditionals to repeatedly perform different actions.  Here’s an example:

int i = 0;
while (i < 5) {
    printf("%d\n", i);
    i++;
}

In this example, the loop will execute five times, with the value of "i" increasing by one each time.  You can also use loops to count things, or to repeat some action a certain number of times.  Here’s an example of counting circles in a display:

